Вот решение:

```javascript
function debounce(fn, delay) {
  let timer;
  return (...args) => {
    clearTimeout(timer);
    timer = setTimeout(() => fn(...args), delay);
  };
}

const onType = debounce((q) => console.log("search", q), 300);
```

Каждый новый вызов сбрасывает таймер, поэтому `fn` выполнится только после паузы в `delay` мс.

Here is a solution:

```javascript
async function getJson(url) {
  const res = await fetch(url);
  if (!res.ok) {
    throw new Error(`HTTP ${res.status}`);
  }
  return res.json();
}

getJson("https://example.com/api").then(console.log).catch(console.error);
```

`fetch` does not reject on 4xx/5xx statuses, so we check `res.ok` ourselves.

Here is a solution:

```python
def binary_search(arr, target):
    lo, hi = 0, len(arr) - 1
    while lo <= hi:
        mid = (lo + hi) // 2
        if arr[mid] == target:
            return mid
        if arr[mid] < target:
            lo = mid + 1
        else:
            hi = mid - 1
    return -1

print(binary_search([1, 3, 5, 7, 9], 7))  # 3
```

Each step discards half of the range, so the complexity is O(log n). The list must be sorted.

